"""A single-stroke vector font for QA previews, so rendering needs no font files.

Glyphs are polylines on a grid whose em is :data:`EM` units, baseline at y=0, cap height
14, x-height 10 and descender -4, with y increasing upward. Each entry is
``(nominal width, [polyline, ...])``.

The nominal width is only used to centre a glyph inside its advance. Advances themselves
come from :mod:`altium_tools.metrics`, which carries the real Times and Helvetica width
sets, so preview text occupies exactly the space Altium will give it. That keeps the
collision test and the picture in agreement without depending on a font being installed.
"""

